        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "The Rossinver Convent was established in 1935 by the Franciscan Sisters of the Atonement. \nThe Property has served as a Convent, Nursing Home and a Guest House.\nThe Franciscan Sisters handed the property over to private ownership around 2005, after which it served as a private dwelling.\n\nRossinver House (former convent) presents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial and historically significant high-profile property.\nLocated on the outskirts of Rossinver Village on the southern shores of Lough Melvin and only 2 miles from the border with Co. Fermanagh.\n\nThis substantial property comprises of a three-storey building of approximately 660 sq.m (7,088 sq.ft.) \nThe ground floor features 2 kitchens, dining room, 3 reception rooms, 2 bedrooms, bathroom, 4 toilets, back entrance, utility room, boiler room. \nThe upper floors comprise of kitchen, reception room, 11 bedrooms, 3 bathrooms, 2 toilets on the third floor are 3 reception rooms bathroom.\nSet on an elevated 2.3 acres site with impressive views of Lough Melvin and the surrounding countryside, the grounds include ample parking and gardens. \nThe property is in reasonable condition, but substantial refurbishment and remodelling would be required to unlock this unique property's full potential.\n\nSubject to obtaining the relevant planning permission, potential commercial uses for the property could include, guesthouse, boutique hotel, culinary school, healthcare facility, nursing home, community building, culture/arts venue, retreat centre, etc. Additionally, the property could be subdivided into several smaller residential units or apartments subject to planning.\n \n\nOutside\n2.3 acres with garage and store room"
      },
